Vendoring notes
---------------
- Each vendored record under records/ is a single WiCE subclaim record stored
  VERBATIM as JSON (label, claim, evidence, supporting_sentences, meta), with every
  non-ASCII code point escaped to its \uXXXX JSON escape so the committed file is
  strictly ASCII (project convention) while JSON.parse reads back the identical
  record.
- The basename of each record file is the WiCE meta.id (e.g. dev00004-1.json).
- The committed derived manifest (eval/__fixtures__/lz-eval-manifest.json) records,
  in its WiCE sources[] entry, the per-vendored-file sha256. The offline drift gate
  (eval/lz-eval-dataset.test.mjs) recomputes those sha256 values and asserts coverage
  and equality, so the manifest and the vendored records can never silently diverge.
